In article <walker.757868684@mits>, walker@mits.mdata.fi (Jukka Lahtinen) writes:
>BTW, you could as well have wished for "3 blessed amulets of life saving".
>You are allowed to wish for 3 anyting (except artifacts, of course).
>
>Disclaimer: I COULD be wrong, but in that case somebody will correct me.

You ARE wrong - the rule is that you may wish for multiple items if they
can occupy one inventory slot (potions, scrolls, gems, food, thrown weapons).
Objects like armor, wands, amulets always occupy individual inventory slots,
(if you find 10 amulets of life saving they will be put into separate slot 
each - it probably has to do with the fact that you can't wear 10 amulets
at once...). Thus you may wish for 3 potions or scrolls, but only one amulet,
ring or piece of armor.
